; The turn indicator is a lens of its own, stacked UNDER the tail lamp on the same stay rather
; than beside it: the outboard slot at 0.81 is the marker's, and red-over-amber is what a real
; trailer rear cluster is. Splitting the tail lens (the Kenney bodies' TURN_FRAC trick) was the
; other way in and is wrong here — these lenses are hand-authored, so a split costs the same four
; scene edits and leaves the brake lamp narrower for it.
